```c
for (i = 1; i < fb->format->num_planes; i++) {
    plane_state->color_plane[i].offset = ~0xfff;
}
```
Reason:
The loop incorrectly sets offsets for only the first few color planes based on the number of planes in the framebuffer format, which can lead to unused color planes not being set to `~0xfff`. This results in stale offsets being used in calculations, particularly in the `skl_check_main_surface()` function, which relies on these offsets to ensure proper positioning of the main surface relative to the auxiliary surface.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = fb->format->num_planes; i < ARRAY_SIZE(plane_state->color_plane); i++) {
    plane_state->color_plane[i].offset = ~0xfff;
}
```
Reason:
This updated loop correctly sets the offsets for all unused color planes to `~0xfff` by iterating from the number of planes in the framebuffer format to the total size of the `color_plane` array. This ensures that all unused color planes are accounted for, preventing stale offsets from affecting the calculations in `skl_check_main_surface()` and maintaining a consistent non-negative `AUX_DIST`.

